# Milestone: v0.10.12-cat-e-activation
# Covers: cross-spec chain: cond watcher fires -> body emits event -> event
#         subscriber fires; at(x > threshold) body emits e!, at(e?) logs.
#         Tests that a rising-edge cond watcher can trigger event dispatch
#         as a downstream effect (spec cross-spec §2.2).
# matrix-row: reactive-at-cond
#
# Activation history: Cat. E re-audit D2 ratified at v0.10.12.  The original
# 'blocked: chain does not propagate' label was unsubstantiated by C-level
# evidence (c_event_emit_async is non-allocating + body-strand-safe + was
# unit-tested via test_event_emit_async.c until the Phase 0 runtime-internals
# test cleanup; no C-level coverage today).  Activated empirically via
# top-level vars read back as values.
#
# Install order: threshold starts at 0, so at(threshold > 3) does not fire
# at install.  The trigger sets it to 10; the drain that follows evaluates
# the condition and runs the at-cond body, which emits e!; the emission
# spawns the at(e?) subscriber body, which sets Realm.log = "event" before
# the next line reads it.

var Realm.log = ""
[00000000] ""

var threshold = 0
[00000001] 0

var e = Event.new()
[00000002] <event>

at (e?) Realm.log = "event"
[00000003] nil

at (threshold > 3) e!
[00000004] nil

var trigger = function() { threshold = 10 }; trigger()
[00000005] 10

Realm.log
[00000006] "event"
